<a target="_new" href="
http://www.gamesradar.com/previews/default.asp?subsectionid=175&articleid=63491&pagetype=2">Mario Sunshine Preview</a><br>
GamesRadar&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
5/21/2002 6:08:48 AM<P>
GamesRadar has posted a preview of Mario Sunshine. Here is a little of what to expect:<p>
"Since we last saw it, Mario Sunshine has gone through a fair number of changes. To start with, there are far more objects and enemies in the massive 3D environments, the water and sun indicators in the corner of the screen have undergone a redesign, and pretty much everything looks that much more colourful and vibrant than the footage we saw at Spaceworld 2001."<br>
<hr>
<a target="_new" href="
http://www.gamequbed.com/previews/gamecube/mario.shtm">Mario Sunshine Preview</a><br>
9/26/2001 6:49:33 AM<P>
Gamequbed gives us their impressions of the upcoming Mario title for the GameCube.<p>
"Nintendo keeps on reinventing all of their franchises, and Mario proves not be different. This is a highly unique title that has all of the ingredients for success. Mario is currently slated for a 2002 Japenese release, and there is no word on a U.S. release. We'll let you know more information about this game as it becomes available!"<br>
<hr>
<a target="_new" href="
http://www.gamingmaxx.com/previews/ngc/marioshn.htm">Mario Sunshine Preview</a><br>
9/24/2001 7:57:22 AM<P>
Gaming Maxx has posted a preview of the upcoming Mario Sunshine for the GameCube.<p>
"Now we go back into waiting for Nintendo to unlock the vault again on the next Mario adventure, but from what we've seen you should be highly anticipating this title. From the gameplay to the music, the whole Mario atmosphere will be there for sure with this game. All that's left to say is, if you don't think it'll be great, tell me the last time a Mario platformer was bad?"<br>
